/target
/dist
Cargo.lock.bak

# The brand system and the working notes stay out of the repository entirely.
#
# Neither is part of the thing being shipped. brand/ is identity work: source
# SVGs, rendered motion, icon sets and concept sheets, several megabytes of it,
# none of which the crate compiles against. notes/ is thinking: the architecture
# sketch, the submission plan, draft posts. Both change on a different clock from
# the code and neither belongs in a reviewer's diff.
#
# One consequence to respect rather than work around: the report renderer must
# not read brand/tokens.css at build or run time. A clone has no brand/, so an
# include_str! against it would fail to build, and a generated report has to be
# self-contained anyway because it gets emailed to an accountant. Inline the few
# token values the report needs as constants in the Rust source.
brand/
notes/

# Rendered motion frames are large and reproducible from the script.
frames_*/
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Local config, never committed. RPC keys and channel credentials live here.
.env
*.local.toml
config.local.*
